Computing – EC2

EC2 = Elastic (C)ompute (C)loud
(two c is coming so EC2)

EC2 is a virtual server provided by AWS.

It gives you computing power without buying a physical computer or server.
You can choose CPU, memory, storage, and operating system based on your requirement.

EC2 can be used to:
Run applications
Run Python programs
Train or process workloads
Host websites
Run backend servers

===========

Simple Example

Instead of buying a powerful computer:

Your Laptop
     ↓
Connect to AWS
     ↓
Create EC2 Virtual Machine
     ↓
Use Computing Power

EC2 = A virtual computer/server in the AWS cloud.

